Overall the asymptotic expression for the determinant can be written as
\begin{equation}
    \mathcal{D}_{\nu}(s,t) \approx \mathcal{A}(\nu, s/t,t) \,
    e^{i\int dk\,\eta_0(k)(s-tk)} .
\end{equation}
Here $\eta_0$ is defined in \eqref{sharp}, while $\mathcal{A}$ contains $C_0$ and the remaining terms of \eqref{as11}. The leading connected correlation on the Euler scale is governed by small $\nu$. At this order, the variation of $\mathcal{A}$ can be neglected and we may set $\mathcal{A}\approx\mathcal{A}(0,s/t,t)=1$.
